<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Q4 GDP growth revised to 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Q4 GDP growth revised to 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch fourth quarter gross domestic product (GDP) growth has been revised up to a year-on-year rate of 3.0 percent from 2.8 percent, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH GDP</p>
<p>		    Q4 96	 Q3 96	 Q2 96	 Q1 96</p>
<p> year-on-year   +3.0 (2.8)  3.1 (3.0)   3.2 (3.1)   1.6 (1.4)</p>
<p>vs previous qtr</p>
<p> (seas. adj.)   +0.5 (0.5)  0.7 (0.6)   1.5 (1.6)   0.3 (0.1)</p>
<p>Note - Figures show real percent changes. Previously announced figures in brackets.  </p>
<p>DUTCH GDP - INVESTMENT IN DETAIL (real pct change yr/yr)</p>
<p>				     1996  Q4 96  Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96</p>
<p>total gross fixed investment  5.5   11.0    8.5    4.1   -1.8</p>
<p>housing			    -0.8    9.1    2.4    2.9  -17.7</p>
<p>other buildings		   3.3    7.2    5.1   13.0  -13.2</p>
<p>roads, waterways etc.	   3.8    4.6    5.8    8.4   -5.8</p>
<p>transport equipment	    -0.9   10.1    0.9  -13.1   -0.6</p>
<p>machinery			  11.4   13.1   18.5    3.1   12.8</p>
<p>DUTCH GDP IN DETAIL</p>
<p> (real pct change yr/yr)	1996  Q4 96  Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96</p>
<p> private consumption	     2.9    2.9    2.6    2.7    3.4</p>
<p> government consumption	  0.5    0.9    0.6    0.5    0.1</p>
<p> business investment	     5.8   12.1    8.9    3.7   -1.1</p>
<p> government investment	   3.1    4.6    5.9    6.9   -6.1</p>
<p> exports goods and services    4.0    4.5    4.6    1.5    5.4</p>
<p> imports goods and services    5.8    6.1    7.1    4.4    5.6</p>
<p>CBS said the volume of gross domestic product for full-year 1996 rose by 2.7 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Gross investment in fixed assets are growing strongly; private consumption is maintaining the favourable trend of the first three quarters while foreign trade clearly picked up in the second half of the year,&quot; CBS said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
